# Cloudflare's observed default for Workers static assets is
# `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate` (an earlier comment here claimed one
# hour; measured on the live site, it is zero). That default made every CSS
# and JS file cost a conditional round-trip on every single navigation.
#
# The tiers: art is addressed by slug and changes only when redrawn, so a day
# plus a week of stale-while-revalidate. Stylesheets and scripts have no
# content hash in their names, so they get one hour with a day of grace:
# an edit reaches every visitor within the hour, and nobody re-fetches the
# same bytes on every click. HTML stays on the revalidating default.

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/og-image.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/favicon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400

/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400

# Hygiene on every response: MIME sniffing off, and referrers shrink to the
# origin when leaving the site.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
